ASM backend migrations
Development uses SQLite: alembic.ini carries no URL, env.py reads ASM_DATABASE_URL.
With ASM_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=true (the default) the API calls create_schema() at
startup, so a dev database needs no Alembic step; migrations remain the source of truth.
Production sets ASM_AUTO_CREATE_SCHEMA=false and runs `alembic upgrade head` before
the API starts; asyncpg URLs are used directly by the async env.py.
Add a revision: ASM_DATABASE_URL=... python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "x",
review the generated ops, then test upgrade head and downgrade -1 on a scratch SQLite file.
Caveat: enum columns are VARCHAR with no CHECK constraint because SAEnum uses
create_constraint=False, so neither create_all nor this migration adds one.
